<title>ITALY: Italy's Ciampi reported meeting Waigel on Sunday.</title>
<headline>Italy's Ciampi reported meeting Waigel on Sunday.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1996-11-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italy's Treasury Minister Carlo Azeglio Ciampi is believed to have met German Finance Minister Theo Waigel on Sunday on a stopover in Germany on his way to an emergency meeting of EU Finance Ministers in Brussels, Italian state agency ANSA reported.</p>
<p>Waigel is not present at the Brussels talks. Bundesbank governor Hans Tietmeyer is the only top level German official attending the meeting.</p>
<p>Europe's top financial policy-makers had to be called in after the EU's monetary committee of central bank and finance ministry officials failed on Saturday to agree on a central parity rate for the lira's return to the EU's exchange rate mechanism (ERM).</p>
</text>
